{"title":"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Similar_to_1,_Diophantine_Equations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Similar to 1, Diophantine Equations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Anh read a book. On the first day she read <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> pages in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> minutes, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers. On the second day Anh read <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> pages in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08e69ae7d33d4b7626acc4b5ec7b4b94f43962b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> minutes. Each day thereafter Anh read one more page than she read on the previous day, and it took her one more minute than on the previous day until she completely read the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc26282a0a5c8c656320dbe7fd616479dfd59a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> page book. It took her a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2902bedd63289eb1e6e5fb0f00ac4a4d35f3c699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> minutes to read the book. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390b15d820099dfc099fbff3cf46b881dc1475ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of days Anh reads for.  Because the difference between the number of pages and minutes Anh reads for each day stays constant and is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be a factor of the total difference, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e46e596fa90201bd383f5ee3150e77b583b626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374-319=55$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" />.  Also note that the number of pages Anh reads is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/4781da5795c202abbda381cab0f8ba7494e70e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dn+\\frac{d(d-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />.  Similarly, the number of minutes she reads for is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f838a721e6a9ace07d21e780a04acf2cc30b1e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dt+\\frac{d(d-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />.  When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is odd (which it must be), both of these numbers are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79030abeb688469b5ffc2e1c4e37fee225a529e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2902bedd63289eb1e6e5fb0f00ac4a4d35f3c699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc26282a0a5c8c656320dbe7fd616479dfd59a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.  The only such numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  We know that Anh reads for at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2794adcdf17eae205211ba8e5b847bb349d68088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Using this, we find that she reads <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79030abeb688469b5ffc2e1c4e37fee225a529e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \"additional\" pages and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79030abeb688469b5ffc2e1c4e37fee225a529e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \"additional\" minutes.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f45921c113ed8ab330030c42795d17a63c5b7e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{374-55}{11}=29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e36a60978fe8a9a436074a9919d06120de4d3fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{319-55}{11}=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"38\" />.  The answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef95cb9729e812753b4639655f8fa8ea814e25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29+24=\\fbox{053}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We could see that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc26282a0a5c8c656320dbe7fd616479dfd59a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2902bedd63289eb1e6e5fb0f00ac4a4d35f3c699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in the outset, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, the quotients, are relatively prime. Both are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a8a0bf43ddaaf1809736227cc935fd31ec4fc8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$average$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"11\" /> number of minutes across the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days, so we need to subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa3f7a27fc66718825be9e7dcd8e9079b9bb1b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor{\\frac{11}{2}}\\right \\rfloor=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"75\" height=\"43\" /> from each to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce181dac76d44321fa1b75df37ce0af27c4b46a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,t)=(29,24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81e9f80b4b608a07303315656e2c907e4c60f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29+24=\\boxed{053}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be equal to the number of days it took to read the book, the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ece7f97f556d5af63003cb94ecbc04def23999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf309c36eae6881bb7012fa1bc7923748c7436c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n+k)(k+1)=748$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/4258bb76a9ddd4175d4bacde0c66f7aeb971620f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2t+k)(k+1)=638$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> We know that both factors must be integers and we see that the only common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31708e7cd43a1757cf31ba9c99f1e1441c2dc7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$748$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f9f13bc8174eb340359809e67095d53dd65a8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$638$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that will get us positive integer solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84c01f25a78d352f0ad6ae7185c25465bbf46c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afd9b066c6c1fb6ef4383cb93bbabe6521c36d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. We then solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> in their respective equations, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295ff30311843c1587c7f72ae3c8025d9aaabd6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+10=68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb3e54fa1ece832295384bbb5fb50466a796aa7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=29$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />  We also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5adb2811de19ca58a0fc642606f047bc063f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t+10=58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c238d9bb51253eec48cee4e4c83bb3a0892f7089.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. Our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81e9f80b4b608a07303315656e2c907e4c60f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29+24=\\boxed{053}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758d1e45533f22bf1eb15100497cb9a1dd2b38f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374=34\\cdot 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e28dbe63da4c3e868ef3d94e6ccf963166b0a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319=29\\cdot 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />. Also, note the sum of an arithmetic series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e3884a4c4a5102b69680b4a372ed4b84975d7ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2n+k}{2} \\cdot b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is our first term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ece7f97f556d5af63003cb94ecbc04def23999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> is our final term, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of terms. Since we know both sequences of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> have the same length, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is prime and shared by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2902bedd63289eb1e6e5fb0f00ac4a4d35f3c699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc26282a0a5c8c656320dbe7fd616479dfd59a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, we deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/6636015bc4d4e9e45aee2e6aeda43041a636c64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />. Thus from here we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f55bfcd252da106547ccb0b28d924ed89e2cbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+k=68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/646bcf0cfbdb1c76a3087afbac1bc31edc66b14e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t+k=58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> by using our other factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Finally, we add the two systems up and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f76bcaa2120daea1fb952d6972ae7021c6231ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t+2k+2n=126$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />. But, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f7bc5e1f0bc96bcae61a30c84bca63dee96bad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />, since the first term has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badf0ecd1ef8289387d8462393438c6e2710ff28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and our last term has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f7bc5e1f0bc96bcae61a30c84bca63dee96bad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />. Plugging this back into our equation we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb08b6f8ae256531ef40c494bc5febf2e239bca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+2t=106 \\implies n+t=\\boxed{053}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"263\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We list two equations:\n\\begin{align*}\nn+(n+1)+...+(n+k)&amp;=374\\\\\nt+(t+1)+...+(t+k)&amp;=319.\n\\end{align*}\nSubtracting the two, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a6fa76a64f322673d530ec86f4f10f81d5ef95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n-t)(k+1)=374-319=55.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" />\nManipulating the first and second equation, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\nn(k+1)+\\frac{k(k+1)}{2}&amp;=374 \\\\\nt(k+1)+\\frac{k(k+1)}{2}&amp;=319.\n\\end{align*}\nWe factor out the common factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\n(k+1)\\left(n+\\frac{k}{2}\\right)&amp;=374 \\\\\n(k+1)\\left(t+\\frac{k}{2}\\right)&amp;=319.\n\\end{align*}\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc26282a0a5c8c656320dbe7fd616479dfd59a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$374$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2902bedd63289eb1e6e5fb0f00ac4a4d35f3c699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> have a GCD of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f480123fdee29c93742d132dcdab8439a72e45d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> now combining this with our equation that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/18840f0648c08f636a4050fe6e2c8fc0c4f527ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-t)(k+1)=55,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> has to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e76ce9da0f428536412a4f539b127c608760686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> Thus, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/1044b1b1fd2399ca188baeaff221b3fcfd4382c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n,t)=(29,24) \\Rightarrow n+t=29+24=\\boxed{053}.\\]\" width=\"338\" height=\"23\" />\nNote: We see that because n-t=5, it becomes impossible for n+k/2 and t+k/2 to both be multiples of 11. Thus, this satisfies our condition. Thus k+1 must be 11 to satisfy the common factor 11 constraint.\n<b>mathboy282</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Similar_to_1.2C_Diophantine_Equations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Similar_to_1,_Diophantine_Equations)\">Solution 6 (Similar to 1, Diophantine Equations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Similar to 1, Diophantine Equations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to be the number of days it takes Ana to read her book. Now, notice that the two sums\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8bacd30547ce5a5b1016d94d79a89f6201d60ea9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{d} n+k-1 =374\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"51\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d437f500e8cbaf1a7fa02ee3d1eeeb76a65cb61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{and}\\]\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/6268f645d540b9e6bc37eb9085f18e2fb8eedda5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{d} t+k-1 = 319\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p><p>Subtraction of the two sums yields \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f8c2823cd50839158309a21116c422f985cedf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d(n-t) = 55\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The possible ordered pairing is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/326e933219f2fdde0ad8cdda8581c8d5219e2c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 5, n-t = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c6ed4588d2a118042c85e22b21358e00a25f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 11, n-t = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeb704d8082e7782b96e9bab17ada0e0b7f89b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 55, n-t = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/835a5aa8593095d91742927fb0c8e0ba70c03b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=1, n-t = 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. Obviously the latter case doesn't work as obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886abf6a9edd7a8847b5c2d39430a2d4e1349d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$373 +374 \\neq 374$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />, and the second to last case won't work as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> would be negative. The first case won't work as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer. The last case gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de0b8f15cfc397f4bfaa2d541f86b5929198f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,t) = (29,24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> which satisfies the constraints so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb4ed9ac58b3ddc54e0778fd471f12b35216cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{053}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I\" title=\"2016 AIME I\">2016 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181210\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 605/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18033/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.